WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.440
<v Odysseus>Come, mother — drink of the blood and know me. It is I, alive, your son.

2
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:24.330
<v Narrator><i>Odysseus describes Penelope's fidelity, Telemachus's position, and Laertes's isolated grief.</i>

3
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:42.220
<v Odysseus>No sickness took you, then. It was longing — longing for me, for my counsels and my gentleness — that stole the honey of your life. My going killed you, mother.

4
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:53.270
<v Narrator><i>Odysseus tries three times to embrace her, but his arms pass through the shade.</i>
